\tag{fdip}
\title{Affine links and exterior matter}
\date{2026-11-17}

\p{An affine link carries a rotation and a translation. A rotation
acts linearly on an internal exterior algebra, whereas adding a
nonzero translation does not. How much of the affine gauge law can
a matter operator on a fixed finite torus retain? The exterior
pairing gives a covariant rotation coupling; a separate exact
translation tests a proposed use of edge vectors as directions.}

